DFTTest at bc5e018 (and yuygfgg/VapourSynth-DFTTest e6f580a, which macOS
arm64 builds) AFTER dfttest-bc5e018-thread-safety.patch: apply that patch
first. Its last hunk is the context of this one (the plugin name line), so
this patch does not apply on its own. VapourBox task #101,
docs/reports/task-101-dfttest-fftw-planning.

dfttestCreate plans its four FFTs (r2c/c2r, 2D or 3D by tbsize) with
FFTW_PATIENT. PATIENT times candidate plans in the running process and keeps
the fastest, and different plans round the floats differently, so the same
script gave one of several pictures depending on the process: a preview and
its encode (two processes) could filter the same frame differently. Task #80
found the same in FFT3DFilter's FFTW_MEASURE. DFTTest has no argument that
selects the planner, so the fix is here.

The patch plans with FFTW_ESTIMATE, which chooses by FFTW's heuristics
alone: one plan per machine, in every process. It also leaves no measured
wisdom in the process for a later ESTIMATE request of the same problem
(FFTW reuses wisdom from a more patient planner). It appends
"; FFTW_ESTIMATE, task #101" to the "(VapourBox: ...)" suffix of the plugin's
name, which is how the deps scripts and the test tell this build from a
thread-safe build that still plans with PATIENT.

Applied by download-deps-{macos,linux}.sh and download-deps-windows.ps1 right
after the thread-safety patch; each build fails if it stops applying.

